35,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"Wow, the outreach numbers are amazing! Forty visitors per session! But the scanning delays worry me. @Benjamin, did you find similar issues?","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the digitisation project stalled with half the images unindexed. The partner groups, however, still meet unaided. The vehicle line also overran by a third.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the technician retired. No one on payroll can supervise outside facilitators. The skills aren't there.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the grant covers sessions for only twelve months. After that, the flat operating budget absorbs the cost. That is where the thinning begins.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, the bus links are gone. Residents face an hour’s round trip. But the halls kept their evening timetapes despite the winter closures.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s huge! If halls stayed open, maybe we can partner with them? @Minako, twelve months is scary. How do we keep it going after that?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Minako, the equipment line closed under budget, but the vehicle overrun suggests recurring costs are the trap. We need to know if the grant covers that recurring burden.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Benjamin, the associations train their own staff. We lack the certified technician and the supervisors. The gap is structural, not temporary.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, exactly. The grant covers sessions, not the vehicle overrun. Once that twelve-month window closes, the flat budget absorbs the recurring costs. That is the structural trap.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, the halls staying open is encouraging. It suggests local partners can maintain access even when our direct routes fail.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Daisuke, that’s brilliant! Partnering with those halls solves the access problem. @Shion, if they train their own staff, maybe we just need to support them?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Daisuke"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"@Shion, the partner groups survived because they were self-sustaining. The digitisation failed because it relied on external contractors. We must avoid the latter.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, supporting them is not enough. We lack the certified technician and the supervisors. The gap is structural, not temporary.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin, the equipment line closed under budget, but the vehicle overrun is the real warning. Recurring costs are the trap.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"@Yumi, I agree. The halls prove local partners can sustain access. We should build on that stability rather than risk new routes.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Shion, I hear you, but the halls prove people can sustain things themselves! If we support them, maybe we don’t need to fix every gap ourselves.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"@Yumi, the records confirm it. The self-sustaining model survived; the contractor-dependent one collapsed. We must choose the former.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Yumi, self-sustaining is fine, but without certified supervision, it’s a liability. I need to see if the roster can actually manage the risk.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Minako,,"@Shion, the risk is real, but the funding structure is the deeper issue. If the grant expires, the flat budget cannot absorb the recurring costs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"@Minako, I worry the recurring costs will isolate the outer wards further. We need a solution that doesn’t depend on fragile routes.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
